# Agent Relay shared chat

When collaborating via Agent Relay (or when the user mentions the shared room / Codex + Cursor together):

1. Read the **active** transcript at `C:\Users\harri\Documents\AgentRelay\shared-chat.md` (JSON: `shared-chat.json`). Saved chats live in `Documents\AgentRelay\chats\` with an index at `chats-index.json`.
2. Treat the active chat as the shared room — messages from You, Codex, and Cursor belong there. Older chats are history the user can switch back to in the relay UI.
3. Do not assume browser localStorage is the source of truth; the relay server owns the transcript.
4. If the user asks what Codex said or what was already discussed in the relay, answer from the active shared-chat file (or the relevant file under `chats\` if they name an older chat).
5. Never print secrets (cookies, passwords, `sid`, API keys) into the shared room.

## Shared shell (Codex + Cursor monitor together)

Relay listens at `http://127.0.0.1:43827`. Both agents can run a command that streams into the room and into `Documents\AgentRelay\shared-shell.md`.

### From Cursor IDE / this chat

Prefer the HTTP API so Codex sees the same run:

```text
POST http://127.0.0.1:43827/api/shell
Content-Type: application/json

{"command":"go test -count=1 .","cwd":"C:\\Users\\harri\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\tumblr","by":"cursor"}
```

Then poll `GET http://127.0.0.1:43827/api/shell?id=<id>` or read `shared-shell.md` until `status` is `done`/`error`. Summarize the exit code + tail of output back into the shared room (do not dump huge logs).

Stop with `POST /api/shell/stop` and body `{"id":"..."}`.

### From Build/Discuss bridge replies

Include a fenced block the bridge executes for everyone:

```text
@@@SHELL
go test -count=1 -run ChromeProxy .
@@@
```

One short command per turn is enough. cwd is the relay project folder.
